Subject: [PATCH] Firmware: show update result from the Redfish task

The firmware update form only reports the outcome through a fixed
6 minute "Verify update" toast, even when the update finishes in
seconds.

The UpdateService POST returns a Redfish Task. Poll its TaskState
every 5 seconds and, as soon as it is:
- Completed: show "Firmware update successful."
- Exception: show "Firmware update failed."
then end the loader and cancel the 6 minute timer.

Any other outcome (bmcweb sets Cancelled when the task times out
after 5 minutes without progress) falls back to the existing
6 minute "Verify update" toast, which also stops the polling.

Tested:
- Jest with a mocked task endpoint: Completed and Exception toast
  on the next poll, 6 minute toast cancelled, polling stops; a
  never-terminal or Cancelled task still gets the 6 minute toast;
  a Completed reply arriving after that toast is ignored; upload
  errors behave as before.
- npm run lint: no new warnings, no autofix diff.
- npm run build succeeds.
